Third-party components
This repository contains components derived from third-party code, which remain subject to their original
licenses: the NeRF backbone in nerf/, encoding.py, activation.py, loss.py and the CUDA extensions gridencoder/,
raymarching/ and shencoder/ (torch-ngp, MIT License, reproduced below); the rasterization-based tracking code in
tracking/ and parts of preprocessing/ (nvdiffrast, NVIDIA Source Code License); tracking/blur.py (torchvision,
BSD 3-Clause License); and nerf/iresnet.py (InsightFace, MIT License). The pretrained ArcFace weights used by
the perceptual loss (assets/backbone.pth) are not included and are subject to the InsightFace model license. The SMPL-X model is not included and is
subject to its own license (https://smpl-x.is.tue.mpg.de); smplx_deformer.py extends the smplx package
(https://github.com/vchoutas/smplx, which is not included) and follows its linear blend skinning code, and is
therefore also subject to the SMPL-X license; the masks in assets/ are defined on the SMPL-X topology
and contain no SMPL-X geometry. DECA (https://github.com/yfeng95/DECA) and
face-alignment (https://github.com/1adrianb/face-alignment) are external dependencies, not included, and are
subject to their own licenses.

